# Crypto Watcher — Backend

> Phase tags (`MVP`, `Phase 1`, `Phase 2`, `Phase 3`, `Final`) cite
> [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.mdc). On-chain logic lives in [CONTRACTS](./CONTRACTS.mdc);
> the API consumed by the UI is in [FRONTEND](./FRONTEND.mdc). Keep this file in
> sync with the actual `apps/api/` implementation (see the docs-sync rule in
> `.cursor/rules/`).

## Tech Stack

From the [README](../README.md): Elysia + Typebox, Kysely + PostgreSQL, Bun runtime,
Elysia testing framework, Docker, Pino + Pino-pretty, `@elysia/openapi` for API docs,
React Email + Nodemailer/SMTP (MailHog locally). Monorepo via Nx + Bun.

## Modular Folder Structure

The API is organized into self-contained feature modules. Each module owns its
routes, service, repository (Kysely), Typebox schemas and tests. Shared concerns
live under `core/` and `shared/`.

```
apps/
└── api/
    ├── src/
    │   ├── main.ts                  # Elysia app bootstrap + plugin wiring
    │   ├── core/                    # Cross-cutting infrastructure
    │   │   ├── db/                  # Kysely instance, types, migrations
    │   │   │   ├── migrations/
    │   │   │   └── schema.ts
    │   │   ├── config/              # env loading + validation
    │   │   ├── logger/              # Pino + pino-pretty
    │   │   ├── auth/                # SIWE/session auth middleware  [MVP]
    │   │   ├── openapi/             # @elysia/openapi setup         [MVP]
    │   │   ├── chain/               # Viem clients, contract reads  [MVP]
    │   │   └── errors/              # error types + handler
    │   ├── modules/                 # Feature modules
    │   │   ├── projects/            # Project catalog + lifecycle   [MVP]
    │   │   │   ├── projects.routes.ts
    │   │   │   ├── projects.service.ts
    │   │   │   ├── projects.repository.ts
    │   │   │   ├── projects.schema.ts   # Typebox
    │   │   │   └── projects.test.ts
    │   │   ├── comments/            # Off-chain public comments     [MVP]
    │   │   ├── auth/                # Wallet auth, sessions         [MVP]
    │   │   ├── users/              # Accounts + profiles           [MVP]
    │   │   ├── voting/             # Vote orchestration/indexing   [MVP]
    │   │   ├── scoring/            # Score computation/read         [MVP]
    │   │   ├── governance/        # Governance proposals/events    [MVP]
    │   │   ├── reputation/        # Reputation read/compute         [MVP→Phase 1]
    │   │   ├── rewards/           # Reward accounting               [Phase 1]
    │   │   ├── notifications/     # In-app + email notifications    [Phase 1]
    │   │   └── webhooks/          # Outbound webhooks               [Phase 3]
    │   ├── shared/                # Shared utils, types, guards
    │   └── emails/                # React Email templates           [MVP]
    ├── test/                      # integration/e2e (Elysia testing framework)
    ├── Dockerfile
    └── package.json
```

> Each module is independent: routes → service → repository. Modules never import
> another module's repository directly; they call the other module's service.

## Modules by Phase

### projects `[MVP]`
- CRUD + lifecycle state machine matching the README flow
  (`In analysis → Ready → Voting → Closed → Analyzed`).
- Read project score for display.
- Community submission queue. `[Phase 2]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- Public off-chain comments (read all, post when authenticated).

### auth + users `[MVP]`
- Wallet connect + SIWE-style verification, session issuance.
- Profile management.
- Role-based access control + admin console. `[Phase 2]`

### voting `[MVP]`
- Index/track on-chain votes from per-project contracts (via `core/chain`).
- Eligibility checks surfaced from the reputation module.
- Subgraph/indexer ingestion replacing direct RPC reads. `[Phase 2]`

### scoring `[MVP]`
- Compute/serve project scores from on-chain tallies + reputation weight.
- Enrich with external risk-data providers. `[Phase 3]`

### governance — launch requirement
- Read/serve on-chain proposals, votes and outcomes from the Governor. `[MVP]`
- Index governance lifecycle events for the UI + notifications. `[MVP]`
- Community proposal support metadata. `[Phase 1]`
- Delegation data. `[Phase 2]`
- Full DAO/treasury data surfaces. `[Final]`

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- Serve eligibility + basic weight. `[MVP]`
- Multi-factor computation + decay jobs. `[Phase 1]`

### rewards `[Phase 1]`
- Reward accounting and slashing records, synced with on-chain distributor.

### notifications `[Phase 1]`
- In-app + email (React Email/Nodemailer) for lifecycle + governance events.

### Platform & scaling
- API docs via `@elysia/openapi`. `[MVP]`
- Observability: Sentry + Better Stack, structured Pino logs. `[MVP]`
- Caching + rate limiting + read scaling. `[Phase 2]`
- Public API, API keys. `[Phase 3]`
- Outbound webhooks. `[Phase 3]`
- Multi-region HA. `[Final]`

## Functional Requirements (by module & phase)

### projects `[MVP]`
- R1: Team can create/update a project and transition its lifecycle state.
- R2: Anyone can list/read projects, filter by state/chain, paginate.
- R3: Each project exposes a computed score once `Analyzed`.
- R4: Community submission queue with team review. `[Phase 2]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- R1: Anyone can read comments for a project.
- R2: Authenticated users can create comments; authors can soft-delete their own.
- R3: Rate limiting + basic spam protection. `[Phase 2]`

### auth + users `[MVP]`
- R1: Wallet connect with SIWE-style nonce → signature → session.
- R2: Sessions are httpOnly-cookie based and revocable.
- R3: Users have a profile (display name, avatar, bio).
- R4: Role-based access control (admin/team/user). `[Phase 2]`

### voting `[MVP]`
- R1: Only reputation-eligible wallets may vote (enforced on-chain, mirrored off-chain).
- R2: Backend indexes on-chain votes per project and serves tallies.
- R3: Vote weight reflects reputation. `[MVP]` Tiered weights `[Phase 1]`.

### scoring `[MVP]`
- R1: Compute score from on-chain tally + reputation weight once voting closes.
- R2: Score is immutable per voting round and versioned.
- R3: Enrich with external risk signals. `[Phase 3]`

### governance `[MVP]` — launch requirement
- R1: Index governance proposals, votes and outcomes from the Governor.
- R2: Serve proposal detail + status to the UI.
- R3: Emit notifications on governance lifecycle events. `[Phase 1]`

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- R1: Serve eligibility + weight for a wallet. `[MVP]`
- R2: Recompute multi-factor reputation on a schedule. `[Phase 1]`

### rewards `[Phase 1]` / notifications `[Phase 1]`
- R1: Record reward/slashing events synced with on-chain distributor.
- R2: Deliver in-app + email notifications for lifecycle/governance events.

## SQL Data Modeling (PostgreSQL via Kysely)

> Migrations live in `core/db/migrations`; types are generated into
> `core/db/schema.ts`. All ids are `uuid` (default `gen_random_uuid()`), all tables
> carry `created_at timestamptz not null default now()` and (where mutable)
> `updated_at timestamptz`. Addresses are stored lowercase `text` (checksummed in UI).

### `users` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| wallet_address | text unique not null | lowercase |
| display_name | text | |
| avatar_url | text | |
| bio | text | |
| role | text not null default 'user' | `user` \| `team` \| `admin` `[Phase 2]` |

### `sessions` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| user_id | uuid fk → users(id) on delete cascade | |
| nonce | text not null | SIWE nonce |
| expires_at | timestamptz not null | |
| revoked_at | timestamptz | nullable |

### `projects` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| slug | text unique not null | |
| name | text not null | |
| description | text | |
| chain_id | integer not null | |
| token_address | text | nullable |
| state | text not null default 'in_analysis' | `in_analysis` \| `ready` \| `voting` \| `closed` \| `analyzed` |
| voting_contract_address | text | set when deployed |
| submitted_by | uuid fk → users(id) | nullable `[Phase 2]` |

Index: `projects(state)`, `projects(chain_id)`.

### `comments` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| project_id | uuid fk → projects(id) on delete cascade | |
| author_id | uuid fk → users(id) | |
| body | text not null | |
| deleted_at | timestamptz | soft delete |

Index: `comments(project_id, created_at desc)`.

### `votes` `[MVP]` (off-chain index of on-chain votes)
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| project_id | uuid fk → projects(id) | |
| voter_address | text not null | lowercase |
| choice | smallint not null | encoded risk/reward choice |
| weight | numeric not null | reputation weight applied |
| tx_hash | text unique not null | on-chain reference |
| block_number | bigint not null | |

Index: unique `(project_id, voter_address, round)`; `votes(project_id)`.

### `scores` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| project_id | uuid fk → projects(id) | |
| round | integer not null | |
| value | numeric not null | final score |
| breakdown | jsonb not null | factor breakdown |

Unique: `(project_id, round)`.

### `reputation` `[MVP → Phase 1]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| wallet_address | text pk | lowercase |
| eligible | boolean not null default false | gating `[MVP]` |
| weight | numeric not null default 0 | |
| factors | jsonb | multi-factor inputs `[Phase 1]` |

### `governance_proposals` `[MVP]`
| column | type | notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| id | uuid pk | |
| onchain_id | text unique not null | Governor proposal id |
| proposer_address | text not null | |
| title | text not null | |
| description | text | |
| state | text not null | `pending` \| `active` \| `succeeded` \| `defeated` \| `executed` |
| start_block | bigint | |
| end_block | bigint | |

### `rewards` `[Phase 1]` / `notifications` `[Phase 1]`
- `rewards(id, wallet_address, project_id, amount, type ['reward'|'slash'], tx_hash)`.
- `notifications(id, user_id, type, payload jsonb, read_at)`.

## REST API Endpoints

> All routes are validated with Typebox; shapes feed `@elysia/openapi`. Base path
> `/api`. `🔒` = authenticated, `👑` = team/admin role `[Phase 2]`.

### auth `[MVP]`
- `POST /auth/nonce` → `{ nonce }` for a wallet address.
- `POST /auth/verify` → verify SIWE signature, set session cookie.
- `POST /auth/logout` 🔒 → revoke session.
- `GET  /auth/me` 🔒 → current user.

### users `[MVP]`
- `GET   /users/:address` → public profile.
- `PATCH /users/me` 🔒 → update own profile.

### projects `[MVP]`
- `GET  /projects` → list (filters: `state`, `chainId`, `q`, `page`, `limit`).
- `GET  /projects/:slug` → project detail (+ latest score).
- `POST /projects` 👑 → create project.
- `PATCH /projects/:id` 👑 → update.
- `POST /projects/:id/transition` 👑 → change lifecycle state.
- `POST /projects/submit` 🔒 → community submission. `[Phase 2]`

### comments `[MVP]`
- `GET    /projects/:id/comments` → list (paginated).
- `POST   /projects/:id/comments` 🔒 → create.
- `DELETE /comments/:id` 🔒 → soft-delete own.

### voting `[MVP]`
- `GET /projects/:id/votes` → tally + per-choice weights.
- `GET /projects/:id/votes/eligibility?address=` → eligibility for a wallet.

### scoring `[MVP]`
- `GET /projects/:id/score` → current score + breakdown.
- `GET /projects/:id/score/history` → per-round scores.

### governance `[MVP]`
- `GET /governance/proposals` → list (filter `state`).
- `GET /governance/proposals/:onchainId` → detail + votes.

### reputation `[MVP → Phase 1]`
- `GET /reputation/:address` → eligibility + weight (+ factors `[Phase 1]`).

### rewards / notifications `[Phase 1]`
- `GET /rewards/:address`, `GET /notifications` 🔒, `POST /notifications/:id/read` 🔒.

### platform
- `GET /openapi.json` + Swagger UI via `@elysia/openapi`. `[MVP]`
- `GET /health` → liveness/readiness. `[MVP]`
- `POST /webhooks/subscriptions` 🔒. `[Phase 3]`

## Typebox Schemas (representative)

> Schemas live in each module's `*.schema.ts` and are the single source for
> validation + OpenAPI. Examples (TypeScript, Typebox):

```ts
// modules/projects/projects.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const ProjectState = Type.Union([
  Type.Literal('in_analysis'), Type.Literal('ready'), Type.Literal('voting'),
  Type.Literal('closed'), Type.Literal('analyzed'),
])

export const Project = Type.Object({
  id: Type.String({ format: 'uuid' }),
  slug: Type.String(),
  name: Type.String({ minLength: 1, maxLength: 120 }),
  description: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  chainId: Type.Integer(),
  tokenAddress: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  state: ProjectState,
  votingContractAddress: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  score: Type.Optional(Type.Number()),
  createdAt: Type.String({ format: 'date-time' }),
})

export const CreateProjectBody = Type.Object({
  name: Type.String({ minLength: 1, maxLength: 120 }),
  description: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  chainId: Type.Integer(),
  tokenAddress: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
})

export const ListProjectsQuery = Type.Object({
  state: Type.Optional(ProjectState),
  chainId: Type.Optional(Type.Integer()),
  q: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  page: Type.Optional(Type.Integer({ minimum: 1, default: 1 })),
  limit: Type.Optional(Type.Integer({ minimum: 1, maximum: 100, default: 20 })),
})
```

```ts
// modules/auth/auth.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const NonceBody = Type.Object({ address: Type.String() })
export const VerifyBody = Type.Object({
  message: Type.String(),
  signature: Type.String(),
})
export const SessionUser = Type.Object({
  id: Type.String({ format: 'uuid' }),
  walletAddress: Type.String(),
  role: Type.Union([Type.Literal('user'), Type.Literal('team'), Type.Literal('admin')]),
})

// modules/comments/comments.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const CreateCommentBody = Type.Object({
  body: Type.String({ minLength: 1, maxLength: 5000 }),
})

// modules/governance/governance.schema.ts  [MVP]
export const Proposal = Type.Object({
  onchainId: Type.String(),
  proposerAddress: Type.String(),
  title: Type.String(),
  description: Type.Optional(Type.String()),
  state: Type.Union([
    Type.Literal('pending'), Type.Literal('active'), Type.Literal('succeeded'),
    Type.Literal('defeated'), Type.Literal('executed'),
  ]),
})
```

## Conventions

- One feature = one folder under `modules/`, with `*.routes.ts`, `*.service.ts`,
  `*.repository.ts`, `*.schema.ts` (Typebox) and `*.test.ts`.
- All request/response shapes validated with Typebox; schemas feed OpenAPI.
- DB access only through Kysely repositories; migrations live in `core/db/migrations`.
- On-chain reads only through `core/chain` (Viem); never read RPC from a module directly.
- Tests with the Elysia testing framework + Bun, mirroring module layout. `[MVP]`
